# A rule whose rate parameter is 0 at load, switched on by an RNF script.
#
# NFinput left out of the System every rule whose base rate was zero at load,
# so "set kon 3" and "update" in an RNF script changed the parameter and nothing
# else: no rule read it. BioNetGen writes every rate as a parameter (a literal 0
# becomes _rateLaw1 = 0), so a later set could reach any of them.
#
# A(s~0) -> A(s~1) at kon, back at koff. From 1000 A(s~0), once kon is set,
#     A1(t) = 1000*kon/(kon+koff)*(1 - exp(-(kon+koff)*t)),
# 736.3 at t = 1 for kon = 3, koff = 1. With the rule left out, A1 stays 0.
begin model
begin parameters
  N0   1000
  kon  0
  koff 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(s~0~1)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(s~0) N0
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules A1 A(s~1)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  on:  A(s~0) -> A(s~1) kon
  off: A(s~1) -> A(s~0) koff
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
writeXML()
end actions
